Day 14 – Time and Distance

📚 Topic

Time and Distance – Aptitude

📌 Key Formulas

- Distance = Speed × Time
- Speed = Distance ÷ Time
- Time = Distance ÷ Speed

Unit Conversion

- 1 hour = 60 minutes
- 1 km = 1000 m
- km/hr → m/s = × 5/18
- m/s → km/hr = × 18/5

Relative Speed

- Opposite Direction = S₁ + S₂
- Same Direction = |S₁ − S₂|

✏️ Example

A car travels at 60 km/hr for 3 hours.

Distance = Speed × Time

= 60 × 3

= 180 km

📝 Practice Questions

1. A train travels at 72 km/hr. How much distance will it cover in 25 minutes?
2. A car covers 240 km in 4 hours. Find its speed.
3. Convert 54 km/hr into m/s.
4. Two cars travel in opposite directions at 40 km/hr and 50 km/hr. Find their relative speed.
5. A person walks at 5 km/hr. How much time will he take to cover 15 km?

🎯 Learning Outcome

Today I learned the basic concepts, formulas, unit conversions, and relative speed in Time and Distance.
